      "<b>The flip carousel.</b> Measured at 30 fps: the incoming card rises to edge-on (90°) by the time it is 30 % of a page from centre, in step with the finger; from there it lets go of position and falls back to flat on a clock — exponential, τ ≈ 120 ms (90 → 55 → 43 → 31 → 23 … → 5° over 330 ms) — so it arrives still turning. Rotation as a pure function of position parks the card edge-on and loses the settle, which is the whole feel. The page itself is easeOutQuad over 450 ms. Drags rubber-band past either end at 0.3 and fling at most one page.",
      "<b>The terminal is CSS 3D, not a drawing.</b> An orthographic plane at <code>rotateX(55°) rotateZ(−45°)</code>, solved from the source frame: the gold card's four corners give the two axes, the black body's four silhouette extremes give the origin (221.5, 285) and the footprint. Body, keys and the printer's half-cylinder are stacked 1-px slices so rounded corners carry down the sides. The card hovers 26 above the far edge — a contactless tap, not a card lying on the keys.",
      "<b>Order button → gooey loader.</b> Beats from the source (tap = 0): the label blurs out in 110 ms at full width; only at 230 ms does the pill snap to 136 wide, in 110 ms. Inside, two grey circles under <code>feGaussianBlur(3.2)</code> + an alpha matrix <code>19 −8</code> merge and split on a 1.15 s swing, starting merged. The caption swaps to 'Confirming your payment…'. The terminal comes in at 2.45 s.",
      "<b>Paid.</b> The card lands at 3.0 s with a 3-px rebound, the check draws in 250 ms at 3.45 s (<code>pathLength=1</code> + dashoffset), title, copy and panel rise 8 px at 3.84 / 3.98 / 4.14 s, buttons at 4.52 s, then the card slides off the near edge.",
      "<b>Receipt.</b> The feed window's top edge is the slot, so the paper is translated up out of view and pulled down — the <i>bottom</i> of the receipt comes out first, as in the source. Speed is modulated, not stepped: <code>q(t) = t − k·sin(2πnt)/(2πn)</code> with n = 23, k = .72 stays monotonic (never backs up) and lands exactly on 1, so the paper surges and hesitates like a thermal feed. 2.4 s feed, 520 ms drop-and-rock off the cutter, then the stamp: in at 2.4× and −34°, blurred, overshoots to .94 and lands at −14° in 280 ms while the paper takes a 3-px jolt. Barcode is real Code 128-B of the receipt number. Torn edge is a 12 × 8 conic-gradient mask tile.",
      "Neutral by design: the source's card-network logo is replaced by the issuer's own wordmark, the holder is a placeholder name. Fonts are self-hosted OFL latin subsets — Plus Jakarta Sans (UI), JetBrains Mono (receipt), Instrument Serif italic (sign-off), 74 KB together.",
      "Walks the whole flow on its own (≈ 24 s) until someone touches it; every screen then works by tap and drag, including back from each step and Print again. Under reduced motion every tween runs in 1 ms, so the flow still works and lands on the same end states.",
