    prompt: "Build a todo tower in vanilla HTML/CSS/JS: a 300×320 room with N white cards (164×36, radius 10, checkbox + text) that are rigid bodies {x, y (up), a, vx, vy, w, hw, hh, invM, invI, friction}. Start them stacked with a sideways offset scaled by slip. Static bodies for the floor and two walls. Fixed-step loop at 240Hz accumulated from requestAnimationFrame: apply gravity (900 + 3300·gravity/100); build contacts by SAT between every card pair and card/wall (choose the least-overlap axis, flip the normal to point A→B, take the two deepest incident corners with their depths); carry pn/pt over from last step's matching points (warm start, re-apply as impulses); then 12 iterations of sequential impulses with normal impulse clamped ≥ 0 plus a Baumgarte bias 0.2/dt·max(0, depth − 0.5) and tangent impulse clamped to ±μ·pn; integrate. A held card has invM .25 and μ 0 and its velocity is set toward the pointer each step (speed min(1800, dist·40)); on release it keeps its velocity. Render with transform: translate(x, −y) rotate(−a). Stop the loop when everything is slower than 2px/s and 0.05rad/s. Parameters: fill, stroke, gravity 0–100, slip 0–100, todos 3–8. Add a bench panel on the right (224px, white, hairline left border): a title with a small uppercase kind, groups labelled SWITCHES and LEVELS, segmented pills for switches and 34px filled bars with a hidden range input for levels; every change re-applies the parameters live. Credit: rebuilt from Bencho by Lorenzo Cabra, block logic MIT.",
